{
  "summary": "This experiment tested the scvi_n200 RNA encoder in a high-performing multimodal multiprofile setup (using imagenet_vit_l image encoder, avgpool aggregation, and weighted fusion), achieving validation accuracy of 0.7062 and F1 of 0.6671, surpassing the previous concat fusion baseline (llm_summary_008). The results suggest the RNA encoder choice may contribute to performance, but the exact impact remains uncertain without direct comparison to other RNA encoders or isolation of other factors like fusion weights. The improvement relative to the pca_n2000-based baseline (llm_summary_008) indicates potential value in scvi_n200, though alternative explanations (e.g., residual training effects) cannot be ruled out."
}

